+
+## Data and runtime reference
+
+The personal website omits repeated explanatory banners and general simulation-details panels. This reference remains with the repository; market selectors, Replay labels, simulated account labels, error messages and source-editing controls retain their meaning.
+
+Historical prices: retained Yahoo Finance one-minute OHLC for 10 Sep 2026, with 390 one-minute bars per instrument. Synthetic prices: scenarios generated by P.Book.
+
+The order book, trading activity and account results are simulated. No live market connection or real orders.
+
+Synthetic contract definitions reference retained Optibook course metadata; the generated prices come from P.Book. This site does not connect to Optibook.
+
+Edit and export strategies in the browser. Python execution requires the local P.Book runtime.
+
+For learning and research, not investment advice.
+
+Presentation cleanup is applied by `scripts/public_clean.py` through the existing demo and quality generators. It removes generic explanation components instead of concealing them with CSS, changes index headers from `#` to `No.`, and versions the changed module URLs while preserving one shared React instance. It does not use the rejected blue-white design.
